          "kind": "text",
          "text": "A lifestyle disease is defined as a condition whose onset and progression are influenced by habits such as diet, exercise, smoking, and drinking. What's less well known is that official guidance explicitly excludes familial (hereditary) conditions from this definition. In other words, even under the same diagnosis name, there are clearly cases caused by something other than lifestyle."
